    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Question\r\n\r\nWarning `(mini.pick) Duplicating mapping keys: caret_start and move_start` for the code (after https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/3b1b65e1e14cd0bf7b4178b38750f4a733e9d4e0):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.pack.add({\r\n  { src = \"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim\" },\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Space>R\", \"<Cmd>restart<CR>\")\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<Space>f\", \"<Cmd>Pick files<CR>\")\r\n\r\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({\r\n  mappings = {\r\n    caret_start = { char = \"<Home>\", func = function() end },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nBy default, `move_start = <C-g>` also sets `alt_chars = { move_start = \"<Home>\" }`. This causes a warning when the `<Home>` key is defined.\r\n\r\nThere's currently no way to disable `alt_chars`, so they probably need to be ignored for the warning. Alternatively, alt keys could be defined directly in the `mappings`, for example: `move_start_alt = \"<Home>\"`.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/59f09943573c5348ca6c88393fa09ce3b66a7818/lua/mini/pick.lua#L2537-L2561\r\n\r\nP.S. Not sure why I didn't create an issue, maybe the weather's just too nice.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.pick</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Warning <code class=\"notranslate\">(mini.pick) Duplicating mapping keys: caret_start and move_start</code> for the code (after <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/3b1b65e1e14cd0bf7b4178b38750f4a733e9d4e0/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/3b1b65e1e14cd0bf7b4178b38750f4a733e9d4e0\"><tt>3b1b65e</tt></a>):</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.pack.add({\n  { src = &quot;https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim&quot; },\n})\n\nvim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;&lt;Space&gt;R&quot;, &quot;&lt;Cmd&gt;restart&lt;CR&gt;&quot;)\nvim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;&lt;Space&gt;f&quot;, &quot;&lt;Cmd&gt;Pick files&lt;CR&gt;&quot;)\n\nrequire(&quot;mini.pick&quot;).setup({\n  mappings = {\n    caret_start = { char = &quot;&lt;Home&gt;&quot;, func = function() end },\n  },\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">pack</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">add</span>({\n  { <span class=\"pl-smi\">src</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n})\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Space&gt;R<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Cmd&gt;restart&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Space&gt;f<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Cmd&gt;Pick files&lt;CR&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.pick<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>({\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">caret_start</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-smi\">char</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>&lt;Home&gt;<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-en\">func</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>() <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span> },\n  },\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">By default, <code class=\"notranslate\">move_start = &lt;C-g&gt;</code> also sets <code class=\"notranslate\">alt_chars = { move_start = \"&lt;Home&gt;\" }</code>. This causes a warning when the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Home&gt;</code> key is defined.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There's currently no way to disable <code class=\"notranslate\">alt_chars</code>, so they probably need to be ignored for the warning. Alternatively, alt keys could be defined directly in the <code class=\"notranslate\">mappings</code>, for example: <code class=\"notranslate\">move_start_alt = \"&lt;Home&gt;\"</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><div class=\"Box Box--condensed my-2\">\n  <div class=\"Box-header f6\">\n    <p class=\"mb-0 text-bold\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/59f09943573c5348ca6c88393fa09ce3b66a7818/lua/mini/pick.lua#L2537-L2561\">mini.nvim/lua/mini/pick.lua</a>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"mb-0 color-fg-muted\">\n        Lines 2537 to 2561\n      in\n      <a data-pjax=\"true\" class=\"commit-tease-sha Link--inTextBlock\" href=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/commit/59f09943573c5348ca6c88393fa09ce3b66a7818\">59f0994</a>\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div itemprop=\"text\" class=\"Box-body p-0 blob-wrapper blob-wrapper-embedded data\">\n    <table class=\"highlight tab-size mb-0 js-file-line-container\" data-tab-size=\"8\" data-paste-markdown-skip=\"\">\n\n        <tbody><tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L2537\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"2537\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC2537\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\"> <span class=\"pl-smi\">H</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">normalize_mappings</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">mappings</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">skip_alternatives</span>) </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L2538\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"2538\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC2538\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\">   <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">res</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> {} </td>\n        </tr>\n\n        <tr class=\"border-0\">\n          <td id=\"L2539\" class=\"blob-num border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default\" data-line-number=\"2539\"></td>\n          <td id=\"LC2539\" class=\"blob-code border-0 tmp-px-3 py-0 color-bg-default blob-code-inner js-file-line\">   <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span